@startuml
title Expense Submission Interaction (Both scopes; proposed boundaries)
autonumber
actor "Group member" as Member
boundary "Swing UI or\nplatform client" as UI
control "Expense application service" as Service
control "Expense and split domain rules" as Domain
database "Persistence adapter" as Store
participant "Notification worker" as Worker

Member -> UI: Enter expense and submit
UI -> Service: Submit request + authenticated principal
Service -> Store: Load group and current memberships
Store --> Service: Group and membership data
Service -> Domain: Validate request and calculate shares
alt invalid or unauthorized
  Domain --> Service: Explicit validation/authorization failure
  Service --> UI: Error result; no expense committed
  UI --> Member: Show understandable message
else valid
  Domain --> Service: Pending expense and exact shares
  Service -> Store: Begin transaction
  Service -> Store: Save expense, shares and approval snapshot
  Service -> Store: Save outbox intent for other eligible members
  Service -> Store: Commit transaction
  Store --> Service: Committed pending expense
  Service --> UI: Pending-review result
  UI --> Member: Show pending status; balances unchanged
  Worker -> Store: Read committed outbox item and resolve recipients
  Store --> Worker: Recipient list excluding submitter
  Worker -> Store: Persist/deliver authorized in-app notices
end
note over Service,Store
  Final approval later atomically changes expense state and writes
  ledger effects. Submission itself never changes balances.
end note
@enduml
